      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The sales quoting process was smooth. Installation of the wind turbine was then dragged out with lots of stories and excuses. When it was finally installed, it turned out they used an older tower and there was not enough clearance for the blades so when the wind picked up a fin flew off luckily not killing anyone in the school. We then had numerous extra charges charged to the school monthly for a monitoring system that was never actually installed. we tried to get them back to fix it, this resulted in them requesting we don't contact them anymore and find someone else to look after the maintenance. When we tried to do this another company refused as the unit was so faultily put together and would never work safely, they had to decommission it after only 2 years. $70 000 of a tiny struggling schools money and AWS did not care and refused to speak to us further, getting quite nasty towards the end. Now 5 years later it is rusted and completely useless and falling apart every time the wind blows.",
